1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,174
Nobody fired a shot there.

2
00:00:02,624 --> 00:00:04,798
Somebody called, and said something.

3
00:00:05,248 --> 00:00:15,683
That is a scene: a character, a few lines, and enough different ways to say them that it does not sound like a recording.

4
00:00:16,133 --> 00:00:21,350
Today you write one, and the station calls your crew with it.

5
00:00:22,550 --> 00:00:27,333
A scene needs a speaker, and a speaker is a character.

6
00:00:27,783 --> 00:00:29,957
You made characters last time.

7
00:00:30,407 --> 00:00:34,320
Mine is Quill, who runs traffic on the station.

8
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:37,813
Look at the word in round brackets.

9
00:00:38,263 --> 00:00:40,002
That is her key.

10
00:00:40,452 --> 00:00:44,365
From here on, nothing calls her Quill, or Harbormaster.

11
00:00:44,815 --> 00:00:47,424
Everything calls her by her key.

12
00:00:47,874 --> 00:00:49,613
Small letters, no spaces.

13
00:00:50,813 --> 00:00:52,552
A new section, Dialogue.

14
00:00:53,002 --> 00:00:58,654
Its key is the word dialogue, in small letters, and that matters later.

15
00:00:59,104 --> 00:01:05,191
Then the scene: three hashes, a name for my own use, and a key.

16
00:01:05,641 --> 00:01:06,946
Speaker: her key.

17
00:01:07,396 --> 00:01:13,048
When: hail, which means this is a call coming in to the ship.

18
00:01:13,498 --> 00:01:16,107
Title: what the call is about.

19
00:01:16,557 --> 00:01:19,600
The crew reads that before they answer.

20
00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:22,224
And then what she says.

21
00:01:23,424 --> 00:01:26,902
Three lines, each starting with a percent sign.

22
00:01:27,352 --> 00:01:29,961
She does not say all three.

23
00:01:30,411 --> 00:01:31,715
She says one.

24
00:01:32,165 --> 00:01:43,035
Each of these is a take: a different way to say the same thing, and the game picks one by chance each time. Three rules.

25
00:01:43,485 --> 00:01:46,963
A take is one line in the file.

26
00:01:47,413 --> 00:01:58,283
If I press Enter in the middle of it, like this, I have made two takes, and one day the crew gets half a sentence.

27
00:01:58,733 --> 00:02:01,341
Takes are alternatives, not a list.

28
00:02:01,791 --> 00:02:11,357
And plain keyboard characters only: no curly quotes, no long dashes, and never a curly bracket at the start of a take.

29
00:02:12,557 --> 00:02:16,035
So how does she say two things? Blocks.

30
00:02:16,485 --> 00:02:20,398
An at sign and her key starts a block.

31
00:02:20,848 --> 00:02:24,761
Three takes in the first, two in the second.

32
00:02:25,211 --> 00:02:31,298
The game takes one from each, so this little scene can read six ways.

33
00:02:31,748 --> 00:02:36,096
The crew reads the first, presses Continue, reads the second.

34
00:02:36,546 --> 00:02:38,720
Her key, not her name.

35
00:02:39,170 --> 00:02:42,648
And one voice in a scene, for now.

36
00:02:43,848 --> 00:02:49,500
A scene is words on a page until the story places the call.

37
00:02:49,950 --> 00:02:54,733
I want it to come when the crew finishes Close Inspection.

38
00:02:55,183 --> 00:02:59,530
So that quest gets one more line: then, reveal ds1_calls.

39
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,720
And here is ds1_calls.

40
00:03:02,170 --> 00:03:14,343
The word Beat, alone on the first line, says this is a moment in the story and not a job, so it stays out of the quest list.

41
00:03:14,793 --> 00:03:17,402
It starts when it is revealed.

42
00:03:17,852 --> 00:03:28,722
And Action is what happens the moment it starts: two spaces, a dash, then who calls, the word hails, and the key of the scene.

43
00:03:29,172 --> 00:03:32,650
Starts when revealed is what makes her wait.

44
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:37,883
Leave it out, and she calls the moment the game begins.

45
00:03:39,083 --> 00:03:40,083
Lint. Clean.

46
00:03:40,533 --> 00:03:43,576
It catches a speaker who is nobody.

47
00:03:44,026 --> 00:03:48,809
It catches a call to a scene that is not there.

48
00:03:49,259 --> 00:03:54,476
It does not catch this: a capital letter in the section key.

49
00:03:54,926 --> 00:03:57,970
Clean, and the call would never come.

50
00:03:58,420 --> 00:04:10,593
So four names get checked by eye: her key, the scene's key, the beat's key, and the two section keys, which have to be exactly characters and dialogue.

51
00:04:11,043 --> 00:04:13,652
The table is on the page.

52
00:04:14,852 --> 00:04:15,852
In close.

53
00:04:16,302 --> 00:04:22,389
The quest completes, and there she is: Harbormaster Quill, about that hulk. Open it.

54
00:04:22,839 --> 00:04:25,448
One of my three openings. Continue.

55
00:04:25,898 --> 00:04:28,507
One of my two closings. Close.

56
00:04:28,957 --> 00:04:31,130
And again, from the start.

57
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:35,493
Same scene, and it may not read the same.

58
00:04:36,693 --> 00:04:41,911
You have a quest that finishes on a timer, from Lecture 8.

59
00:04:42,361 --> 00:04:48,883
Write a second scene, and have that quest reveal a second beat that calls it.

60
00:04:49,333 --> 00:04:52,811
Next time the crew gets to answer back.
